  "claim_short": "The conjecture that O'Neill's M-bundle section theorem extends from m=1 to all m>=2 is false. For every integer m>=4, the packet constructs a nontrivial, Glaeser-stable, proper, consistent M-bundle over the unit circle in R^3. Its Grassmannian bundle is the constant singleton horizontal plane, but it has no manifold section.",
